diff --git a/objdiff-core/tests/data/ppc/metadata/README.md b/objdiff-core/tests/data/ppc/metadata/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..bbe75ebb4d52fe2a59c33277793f5e8b66a70d50
--- /dev/null
+++ b/objdiff-core/tests/data/ppc/metadata/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+Synthetic PowerPC exception metadata fixtures; no retail code is included.
+
+Regenerate each object with GNU binutils:
+
+    powerpc-eabi-as -mgekko -o target.o target.s
+    powerpc-eabi-as -mgekko -o source.o source.s
+    powerpc-eabi-as -mgekko -o shared.o shared.s
+    powerpc-eabi-as -mgekko -o wrong_owner.o wrong_owner.s
+
+The source contains two unused functions before fixtureMain; the target contains
+only fixtureMain. The exception record names and object offsets differ, but the
+function, unwind bytes, index length, and index relocations match. Metadata table
+symbols are global to preserve direct symbol relocations in GNU as output, as
+used by the CodeWarrior exception decoder. The shared fixture points two index
+entries at one table; wrong_owner associates the final entry with unusedA.
